Relationship to TimiGP
----------------------

InterMeta extends the directional gene-pair prognosis framework implemented by
TimiGP to metabolic pathway analysis. The supplied local upstream snapshot is
labelled TimiGP 1.3.0 and identifies Chenyang Skylar Li as its author. A
94-file full-tree SHA-256 comparison matches the snapshot exactly to the
official TimiGP tag v1.3.0 at commit
9a527dd7dfe18c3155647d57c4392dad977ff13f.

Upstream project: https://github.com/CSkylarL/TimiGP
Related article: https://doi.org/10.1016/j.xcrm.2023.101121

The supplied TimiGP snapshot contains the GNU General Public License version 3
text. InterMeta therefore retains the package-level GPL-3 license and includes
the license text in COPYING. This notice records provenance and does not add
any restriction to the GPL. In particular, an upstream README phrase about
intended research use is not imposed as an additional InterMeta license term.
InterMeta distributes its adapted code under GPL version 3 and retains the
upstream license text, attribution, and modification notices. No separate
permission requirement is added by this notice. The upstream project remains
the source of its own copyright and licensing statements.

Code mapping
------------

* R/Chord.R was adapted from the TimiGP chord-diagram implementation.
* R/Cox.R was adapted from the TimiGP Cox implementation.
* Portions of R/InterMeta.R were adapted from TimiGP preprocessing, pairwise,
  enrichment, permutation, network, dot-plot, and favorability code.

InterMeta modifications through 2026-11-03 include metabolic pathway gene-set
support, stricter input and result validation, a single TimiGP-legacy
analysis mode (since 1.1.4), compact result retention, internal resampling/stability
analysis, and an optional reproducible AI-assisted literature synthesis layer.

The upstream author is listed as a contributor in DESCRIPTION to distinguish
source-code attribution from authorship of the InterMeta manuscript. Final
paper authorship, institutional affiliations, and copyright ownership will be
recorded separately when confirmed.

Data
----

The bundled TCGA-PRAD prognosis and normalized bulk transcriptomic source
tables were downloaded from PCaDB
(http://bioinfo.jialab-ucr.org/PCaDB/; source repository
https://github.com/rli012/PCaDB; DOI 10.1101/2021.06.29.449134). InterMeta
retains the aligned 463-sample prognosis cohort and 1,260-gene metabolic
expression subset used by its public examples. The exact source-input
fingerprints and analysis lineage are stored in InterMetaPRADProvenance.
For InterMeta 1.1.3, the bundled permutation-FDR column was republished from a
fresh no-checkpoint workflow that refitted the Cox models and reran 100
TimiGP-legacy annotation permutations. The historical enrichment file was
used only to verify numerical agreement. The provenance object records the
accepted run identifier and SHA-256 values for its supporting pre-publication
candidate archive, workflow script, complete output manifest, and original
input files. The run did not independently record an archive/core-code hash,
so the archive is not represented as a cryptographic identity of the executing
installation.

Database-derived data can have terms different from the package's code
license. See extdata/metabolic-genesets/PROVENANCE.md and the package dataset
documentation. The GPL-3 label must not be read as an assertion that every
third-party database extract is itself licensed under GPL-3.
